invariant: INV-11
file: quic_packet.c
catches: quic_test
reason: quic_packet_seal keeps the Key Phase bit the caller's header
  holds instead of the key_phase it takes, so a caller who never set the
  bit after a key update sends packets that name the old phase, and the
  peer opens them with the wrong keys. bin/quic_test seals Appendix A.5's
  header, whose bit is clear, under key_phase 1 and requires it to open
  under the current set of phase 1.

--- old
    uint8_t phase = (uint8_t)((key_phase & 1U) << QUIC_KEY_PHASE_SHIFT);
--- new
    (void)key_phase;
    uint8_t phase = (uint8_t)(hdr[0] & QUIC_KEY_PHASE_BIT);
